 "headline": "On the single cell of one lattice step and one tick, each of the 15800 cuttings that reach the floor of the adjacency cost offers a switch for every one of the 120 regions it fills, and those switches are not independent: free switch behaviour survives only to dimension two, 54912 of the 273936 pairs a cutting offers at once share a piece, and 9320 of the cuttings form one connected object under the smallest move. In place of independence the population carries a two sided charge that is a sum of a weight over a cutting's own pieces, reversed by every one of the 46128 smallest moves and kept by every one of the 31968 moves on six pieces; asking instead for reversal at six pieces has no solution over the field with two elements. The partition it names, of sizes 7704 and 8096, is determined, and no single region demand is load bearing while dropping any one of the 5 symmetry families of regions lowers the rank. A core of 48 cuttings admits no cost keeping move on eight pieces or fewer, and all 48 sit on the smaller side of the charge.",
